From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-m5 <omarchy-m5@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:51:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] soc: apple: rtkit: wait 10 s for the boot handshake

Ported from omarchy-m5 patches/linux/0010. On J714s/T6050 with all 15
cores online, nvme-apple logged "ANS did not boot" / -62 about 1.07 s
after RTKit init, leaving the root disk missing; ANS firmware sometimes
needs ~3 s to answer. Workaround from rolotrealanis98/m5pro-linux patch
0016; applies to every RTKit coprocessor.

integration/aurora also has a polled wait (apple,sync-syslog-ack) with
its own 1 s deadline; it uses the same constant.
---
 drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
index 536ba515f..5a55aaeb1 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
@@ -1480,6 +1480,14 @@ struct apple_rtkit *apple_rtkit_init_adopted(struct device *dev, void *cookie,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_rtkit_init_adopted);
 
+/*
+ * omarchy-m5: T6050's ANS firmware sometimes needs ~3 s to answer the RTKit
+ * handshake on an all-core boot, so 1 s leaves the root disk missing.
+ * Workaround from rolotrealanis98/m5pro-linux; it applies to every RTKit
+ * coprocessor, not just ANS.
+ */
+#define APPLE_RTKIT_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS 10000
+
 static int apple_rtkit_wait_for_completion(struct completion *c);
 
 /*
@@ -1496,7 +1504,7 @@ static int apple_rtkit_wait(struct apple_rtkit *rtk, struct completion *c)
 	if (!rtk->sync_syslog_ack)
 		return apple_rtkit_wait_for_completion(c);
 
-	timeout = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(1000);
+	timeout = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_RTKIT_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS);
 	do {
 		ret = apple_rtkit_poll(rtk);
 		if (ret < 0)
@@ -1529,7 +1537,7 @@ static int apple_rtkit_wait_for_completion(struct completion *c)
 	long t;
 
 	t = wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(c,
-						      msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
+			msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_RTKIT_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS));
 	if (t < 0)
 		return t;
 	else if (t == 0)
